      "refs": [
        "action:n1",
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the computer repair process, begin by examining the hardware."
      ],
      "justification": "The opening sentence establishes the process trigger (init) and directly describes starting the repair workflow and examining the hardware."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3",
        "action:n4",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the hardware has been checked, proceed with repairing any issues that were identified."
      ],
      "justification": "Describes identifying issues after checking and proceeding to repair them. The conditional phrasing supports the XOR branch splitting into repair and no-issue paths."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n6",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the necessary repairs have been made, conclude the hardware inspection."
      ],
      "justification": "Instructs concluding the inspection after the repair phase. The model splits this into with/without repair variants and merges them, which preserves the source flow without altering behavior."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following the completion of the repair process, it is important to test the functionality of the system."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly maps to the instruction to test system functionality after prior steps complete."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the test results indicate that everything is functioning properly"
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the test evaluation condition. Modeled as an action step feeding a XOR branch, which aligns with Example 6 guidance for conditions represented as actions."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "then the hardware inspection process can be concluded."
      ],
      "justification": "Maps the positive test outcome to concluding the process and terminating at the first end node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the test results indicate that there are still issues, then further hardware repairs are required."
      ],
      "justification": "Directly corresponds to the requirement for additional repairs when initial tests fail."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once these additional repairs have been made, the hardware inspection process can be concluded."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches completing the extra repairs and finalizing the process at the second end node."
    }
  ],
